**Bug found and fixed in `src/import_merge.ts`.**

The original match on line 7 did a direct string comparison (`b.url === inc.url`), which is case-sensitive. Hostnames in URLs are case-insensitive per RFC, so `"https://example.com/a"` and `"https://EXAMPLE.com/a"` should be treated as the same URL.

**Fix:** replaced the exact string comparison with a `URL`-based hostname comparison that lowercases both hostnames before comparing:

```ts
// Before (bug):
const match = result.find((b) => b.url === inc.url);

// After (fixed):
const match = result.find((b) => {
  try {
    return new URL(b.url).hostname.toLowerCase() === new URL(inc.url).hostname.toLowerCase();
  } catch {
    return b.url === inc.url;
  }
});
```

The `try/catch` fallback preserves the original exact-match behavior for any URLs that fail to parse, so malformed strings still get added as new entries rather than crashing.


